{"title":"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two of the altitudes of the scalene triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \nIf the length of the third altitude is also an integer, what is the biggest it can be?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/6986066a96c1dd189fe2c025c134d5c2543b9e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 7\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"435\" height=\"17\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume we have a scalene triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Arbitrarily, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> be the height to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the height to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Due to area equivalences, the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> must be three times the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Let the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, thus making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d3592aaddfb37d34cee7c9bbcb7a0e71fdbb16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 3x$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, setting the final height to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we note that (by area equivalence) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7702a319373ecfb5048bf08b94e46a1a2f9cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC \\cdot h}{2} = \\frac{3x \\cdot 4}{2} = 6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"170\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3e559926101d12d9953799615a8d2212acc01e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\frac{12x}{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" />. We note that to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we must minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Using the triangle inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2dfa48470384e5a84d85c4215236cad6bfc97635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC + AB &gt; AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67c7d9809c3b092549718a180c9273f3011e473.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC + x &gt; 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07cbcd7bcdc46ad35e5d48f1d62b6278097b4797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC &gt; 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />. The minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, which would output <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/2777d9c2d889051156950faa055367dd36d906a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. However, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> must be larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, the minimum integer height must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The reciprocals of the altitudes of a triangle themselves form a triangle - this can be easily proven. Let our desired altitude be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9abe6e181feb88a291a6096e6f2af1d2ee61895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}&lt;\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc53b0797a12d17273b1496cdffc030ef0a77bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e077568506b292efc96d8995bb922dd9be51ce1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a}&gt;\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{12}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e242ebb6fb103e16ddf90007c2771b3fecef95c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore the maximum integral value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is 5.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME\" title=\"1986 AHSME\">1986 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175459\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 256/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6594/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.477      1 -total\n 57.38%    7.159      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 40.17%    5.012      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13762:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017175459 and revision id 110729. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}